# 0085-field-report-background-build-screen-queue-lag-downloads-space.patch -- the owner's field report on the IPA of 2026-11-21 21:59 and the logs of two more runs (read in ~/Downloads,
# never copied): the build kept in the background, the build screen, the queue during a build, the lag, the cloud listing, the download meter, the free space, the cover badges.
# Applies after 0084. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# B / I. THE BACKGROUND TASK (GameAppBackground.cs). From the log: the BGContinuedProcessingTask was submitted from the foreground at the build's start, accepted and started (its id is
#   `<bundle id>.build.<n>`, permitted by Info.plist's `<bundle id>.build.*`: the start line proves it), and EXPIRED at the start of stage 3, ~90 s later. Its bar came from
#   GameAppUi.ParseStage, which moves only for the rewrite's modules and the "(N/M shaders)" count: through stage 1 (75 s of "unpacking 2.3 of 26.2 GB") and the reading of the shaders
#   ("progress: N/M" lines) it never moved, and iOS expires a continued-processing task whose progress stalls. The expiration then asked the chain to PAUSE (0065): during a read nothing can
#   stop, the request stayed raised (and remembered by the StopMachine during the .nsz extraction) and paused the build later by itself (South Park: "paused before the chain started",
#   although the owner was back). NOW: the bar is BuildProgress.Fraction (stage 1's unpacking, stage 3's reading counter, then the translation), with BackgroundHeartbeat (one unit more every
#   3 s without news, never past the stage's end, never backwards); an expiration pauses only while the shaders are TRANSLATED (ExpirationPolicy: the chain stops after the current one),
#   elsewhere it is logged and the build goes on while iOS lets the process run; a pause iOS asked for that has not taken effect is WITHDRAWN when the person comes back
#   (StopMachine.WithdrawPause, gameapp_request_stop(0)); only the person's own Pause is never withdrawn. The log says what iOS did: "task <id> submitted", "accepted by iOS", "started by
#   iOS N s after its submission", "iOS expired task <id> N s after its submission (its bar at U of 10000, last moved S s before; <stage>)".
# A / L. THE BUILD SCREEN (GameAppLibrary.cs GameBuildViewController): (1) Pause and Cancel were in the scroll, under the live log, 48 pt, while Notify me / Close were a fixed bottom row
#   (56 pt): they ended half under it and were HIDDEN whenever they could not act (a stop being honoured): now one fixed bottom bar, two rows of the same 52 pt pills (#25252b with a hairline,
#   the accent only for the primary), Pause / Cancel always there while it runs, off when they cannot act (BuildScreenButtons). (2) the cover square was the name's colour (blue): the cover,
#   else #25252b with the initials. (3) "STEP 2 OF 5 · 0% · Profile": a .nup's stage 1 is the package's read, which BuildSteps took for "Prepare the profile" (stage k = step k): it is "Read
#   the game" now (BuildProgress.StepLine) and the ring follows the unpacking and the reading. (L) a new run starts with no stage line (South Park's screen showed Zelda's "8938/42848 shaders").
# D. THE QUEUE DURING A BUILD: the menu's "Add to the build queue" was dropped while a build ran and every Build button was off: now a game's Build is "Add to queue" while another builds
#   (LibraryActions.Label / Enabled), the menu keeps its entry, AddToBuildQueue says when the game is the one building or already queued (QueueRule), and during a build it wants the queue
#   so the game starts after the current build (QueueBuildEnded's next).
# E / J / K. THE LAG (the logs: "launch-profile: GatherFacts 95-257", "RefreshScreen 290-437", "log rebuild 320-335", "storage/shadercache 1848-4771" ms): GatherFacts' slow parts are cached
#   (TtlCache: the signature's entitlements once, the identity 30 s and invalidated by an import, the address space 10 s); the log page is redrawn at most once a second (400 ms kept the
#   main thread busy during a build); while the GAME is on screen nothing periodic runs on the main thread (no ticker work, no log tailing into hidden views: read from where it was once the
#   game ends, no screen refresh: done when it ends, no cloud listing) and the log says "game on screen: app timers and cloud work paused"; no folder walk (FolderSizes, on a worker)
#   during a build or a game: measured again when it ends (the cached sizes stay shown). NOT DONE: the live log's table is still rebuilt (bounded, once a second at most), not appended.
# C. THE CLOUD LISTING: it ran (a new SSH connection) at every return to the app, during a build too: now at the launch, on the refresh button, or when 15 minutes old, never while a build or a
#   download runs (CloudRelist); ONE shared NAS session while the app is active (Nas.WithShared: the listing and the covers; closed when the app goes to the background).
# F. DOWNLOADS: "1.2 of 4.8 GB · 38 MB/s · 1 min 35 s left" (the carousel's line, the Build tab's row) and "Downloading 37 % · 38 MB/s · 1:35" (a card, a cover's badge): DownloadMeter (an
